      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Your pain is real, and it’s understandable to feel empty after watching someone you love deteriorate despite your best efforts. While hotlines can feel scripted, the people on the other end are trained to listen without judgment and can help you find concrete steps to cope right now. If you can, try reaching out to a therapist, a grief support group, or a close friend who knows your story—sometimes sharing the raw details can break through the numbness. You don’t have to carry this weight alone; there are people who want to help you carry it.",
